---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { decks } from '../../lib/decks';
---
<Base title="AQA A-level Environmental Science flashcards: key terms and definitions by topic" description="Free flashcards for AQA A-level Environmental Science: the key terms and definitions for each topic, with notes on how each is asked, spaced repetition saved in your browser, and a define-it drill from real definition questions." context="flashcards" leadLine="Know the definitions but still dropping marks on the data questions? That's what a tutor fixes.">
  <h1>Flashcards</h1>
  <p>Key terms and definitions for each topic as flip cards, with spaced repetition saved in your browser. Each card carries a note on how the term is asked and marked. Environmental Science has a large vocabulary and the mark schemes want the precise term. Decks for the remaining topics are being written; the <a href="/practice/define/">define-it drill</a> already covers every real definition question.</p>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Topic</th><th>Terms</th><th>Drill</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{decks.map((d) => <tr><td><a href={`/questions/${d.topic}/`}>{d.name}</a></td><td><a href={`/questions/${d.topic}/terms/`}>{d.terms.length} terms</a></td><td><a href="/practice/define/">Define it</a></td></tr>)}</tbody>
  </table></div>
  <h2>How to use them</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Say the answer out loud before you flip. Then be honest with "Knew it" or "Didn't know it": the cards you miss come back every round, the ones you know come back less often.</li>
    <li>A definition that would score full marks in the exam is the target: the term's meaning in one precise sentence, with an example where the question asks for one.</li>
    <li>"Print all" on any deck gives you paper cards.</li>
  </ul>
</Base>
